    "body": "Stopped after two quick-gate failures. Claim released.\n\nBoth runs of cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main fail this test:\na_tapered_punch_is_refused_at_post_while_the_file_states_no_guide_heights\n\nThe test fails at crates/app/tests/sodick_alc400g.rs:145, before the post runs.\nCreateOperation rejects the requested taper because the machine has no edm.lower_guide_z and edm.upper_guide_z.\nThe exact test also fails with the original post from upstream/main 62e1d36a.\nI did not change this unrelated test or bypass the gate.\n\nI reproduced a separate refusal gap within this issue's scope.\nWireU or WireV before the initial rapid produces no warning and allows T91, C110, and G01 output.\nThe local fix makes onRapid refuse the guide offset and disable cutting for that section.\nIt keeps the explicit 4-axis refusal.\n\nAll six tests in crates/post/tests/sodick_four_axis.rs pass with the fix.\nThe two rapid-placement tests and the section-reset test fail with the original post.\nThey also fail when I remove only sectionOk = false from the new guard.\nBoth mutations pass again after I restore the fix.\nThe post suites and cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings pass.\nNo golden files changed.\n\nSodick's 1998 manual confirms that U/V are offsets from X/Y.\nIt also defines TP and TN as the bottom and top workpiece planes above the table.\nSources: https://www.easymanua.ls/sodick/a600/manual?p=58 and https://www.easymanua.ls/sodick/a320d/manual?p=89\nCamcraft's guided stream instead carries physical guide coordinates.\nThe machine schema has no table datum, and this stream does not carry the two original workpiece-plane coordinates.\nI retained the refusal because copying those guide offsets into G74 does not establish the required plane conversion.\n\nThe uncommitted patch remains on local branch issue/1497-sodick-four-axis.\nWorktree: /home/mikekinney/Camcraft/.claude/worktrees/issue-1497\nLogs remain under /tmp/1497-*.log and are not committed.\nNo push or PR was made. Step 8 was not started.\n",
